WEBVTT

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:20.040
Rental Magica

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.430
Is he an acquaintance of yours, Honami?

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.300
Um, more like my senior than an acquaintance.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.230
What taboo is he accused of breaking?

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:56.400
The word from The Association is that
Astral is hiding some sort of major secret.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.880
It could lead to a cure for his eye.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.180
Cure... Icchan's?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.090
Now that this has happened,

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.030
it looks like I also need to tell
you two about the dragon.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:18.230
All of the eye patch's
function has been destroyed.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.090
It would be nearly impossible for even an
expert mage to wipe away the impurity itself.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.760
But a dragon is an entirely different matter.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.930
Icchan's eye can be cured.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.770
Icchan's eye...

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.910
Episode 23
CHANGELING

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.580
Dragon?

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:13.320
As in a covered-with-scales-type dragon?

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.020
No.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.960
The type of dragon I'm talking about...

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.030
...is a nature spirit which embodies
a natural phenomenon.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.360
I've heard of them.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.360
They occur when natural phenomena
like storms and typhoons...

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.700
...are disrupted by spell power, right?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.870
The president saw a fragment of it
as a child with his Glam Sight.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.370
When it happened,

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.340
the sleeping dragon awakened.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.450
I was just a rookie when it happened
and wasn't directly involved,

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:44.020
but in order for Sekiren and Judaix
to seal the dragon away,

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.150
I heard they cast barriers.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:52.220
But the spell power of Glam Sight
was far more powerful than we imagined.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.460
Despite the barriers,

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.200
a path between Glam Sight and the
dragon fragment had been established,

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.170
and each time the president has used it,

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.430
the fragment has slowly been stimulated.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.440
Besides that, The Association
has grown suspicious...

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.300
...and has made its own move.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.080
Somebody is timing this well
to break the barriers...

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.670
...and once more draw out the
stimulated dragon fragment.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.480
Somebody?

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:20.020
Byakko, Suzaku, Seiryu, Genbu,

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.220
I've a task for you.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:26.620
First of all, we need to find
either the president or Honami.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:30.130
One becomes two, two becomes four.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:32.660
Four becomes eight, eight becomes sixteen.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.500
From the great whole are born the two rites.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.240
From the two rites come the four emblems.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.240
From the four emblems come
the eight signs of divination.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.970
From the eight signs come
the sixty-four great signs.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:55.520
The situation has radically changed
since you made contact with Astral.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.290
What is the meaning of this?

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.630
As things stand,

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.320
The Association cannot simply
ignore this dragon.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:05.630
I'm afraid that Astral may have
sensed The Association's moves...

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.430
...and sped up their own plans.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:12.740
However, I think this may be the best
opportunity for The Association...

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.340
...to rid itself of the eyesore
that Astral has become.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:18.970
Fin Cruda, you seem to misunderstand us.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.550
The Association functions to
maintain order in this world.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.050
We must never forget to maintain
our position of neutrality.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:29.860
Ah, forgive me.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.530
But could you at least give
me until tomorrow morning?

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.560
I promise that I can deliver some result by then.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.300
Tomorrow morning.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.270
We will wait only until then.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.760
I appreciate the latitude you're allowing me.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.340
That mere changeling...

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.650
Adelicia Lenn Mathers.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.950
The demon Shax.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.820
Its power is to find that which is hidden.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.160
Am I what you're looking for?

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:13.920
I was careless before,
not seeing that you were a mage.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:23.340
It's common for mages to cloak
their aura, but you're different.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.410
You seem to do it unintentionally,
as though it's natural to do.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:31.810
Either you're extremely incompetent,
or an extremely high-level mage.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.950
The extremely incompetent one
is Astral's president, isn't it?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.150
In the half a day since we met,
the city's fallen asleep,

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.130
and there's this mist.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.830
I doubt it's a coincidence!

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.600
The greatest magic performed by the now-extinct
Druids who practiced Celtic magic...

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.370
...was to cover an entire
kingdom with fog, wasn't it?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.700
And wasn't a dragon also
involved in that lore?

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.670
I salute the head of Goetia.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.710
I didn't anticipate that you'd try to interfere.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.650
This mist is dragon's breath, isn't it?

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:05.040
Hail!

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.180
Unfortunately, I'm used to that from Honami!

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.290
Forneus!

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:12.390
Shax!

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:18.690
Hail!

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.330
He didn't even recite a spell!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.030
Hail!

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.870
This speed!

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.200
Is this really the same Celtic magic
that Honami practices?!

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.650
What are you scheming?!

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.050
"Scheming" has such an ugly ring to it.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:41.490
All I want is to grant someone's desire.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:43.190
Someone's desire?

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:48.000
Itsuki's Glam Sight was
contaminated to such an extent...

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.960
...because he saw a fragment of
a dragon when he was a child.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.800
Honami blames herself for it.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.570
Honami?!

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.750
If only she hadn't goaded Itsuki to follow her...

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:16.920
If only he hadn't played decoy to save her...

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:23.790
Adelicia!

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:37.410
Adelicia!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.410
Adelicia!

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.550
You're hurt!

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:45.450
I'm fine.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.680
This is nothing.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:49.360
Brace yourself, please.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:51.820
Are you all right?

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.060
Itsuki!

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.730
I missed her vital spot.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:00.000
Are you the one behind all this?

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.830
This is all your doing?

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.670
The fog? Destroying my eyepatch?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.300
What if it is?

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:08.770
But why?

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.370
Because it's what Honami wants.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:16.150
You're lying. Honami would never!

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:25.690
Because she wants to cure your eye.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:33.730
She has for a long time,
although you seem to have forgotten.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:35.700
What do you mean?

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.090
There's no point talking any more.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:39.730
Come forth, Eligor!

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:42.600
The mighty knight who leads 60 legions!

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:50.010
Young Master!

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:54.480
Hail!

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.790
Sekiren, below you!

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:01.330
Nice try.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:02.430
You!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.570
Sekiren!

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:12.400
Sekiren!

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:13.560
What's wrong?

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:16.310
Won't you show me your Glam Sight?

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:18.380
Itsuki!

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:23.070
Do you see the same color that I see?

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:28.020
That's all I've wanted to
know ever since I returned.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:29.850
Returned?

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:42.500
You see...

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.430
I'm a changeling.

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:51.200
You see...

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.610
I'm a changling.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:55.950
Now that I've returned,

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.890
I fear that I'll always be alone, no matter what.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:00.780
So I want a place for myself.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.250
We want people to need us.

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.220
So, isn't it natural then
to grant someone's desire?

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.130
We wish to be needed more than anyone else.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.530
The dragon's just a bonus for me.
What I truly desired was to meet you...

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:18.400
To meet the only other me
who possesses Glam Sight.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:24.170
Itsuki!

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.150
Itsuki!

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.420
Icchan... wait for me.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.820
I swear, I'll cure you.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:56.870
Itsuki!

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.820
It seems that preparations for
the ceremony have been made.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.620
Where is Honami?

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:12.520
If I told you, you'd interfere, wouldn't you?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.730
Besides, I don't think she wants
a visit from you right now.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:20.720
Honami knew about your eye
from the start, didn't she?

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.960
That's why she sought out your teaching.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:28.640
Honami has always wanted to atone
for what she did to Itsuki.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:31.670
That's likely all that she lives for.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.340
That's why I want to grant her desire.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.890
Why do I sense no animosity from him?

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:42.690
Everything in him seems transparent and pure.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.460
Almost close to... good will?

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:46.720
Good will is like magic.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.230
It comes about by exchanging
something for another.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.260
Why are you here?

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.930
For Goetia's sake? Or for Itsuki's?

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:00.040
I see.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:02.130
But that's a lie, isn't it?

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.750
So long as you remain a witch,

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.310
you have nothing to devote to another person.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:12.750
You gave up all of that for the
demons and sorcery, didn't you?

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.910
He has no intent.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:17.120
He's not inducing this in me.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:20.420
He's simply drawing out my own fears.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.890
Not to mention that you are
the Princess of Solomon.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:27.290
A successor to the contract with the demons.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:32.740
Just a cog in the machine that hands
that contract down to the future.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.770
It's not a lie. It's not a deception.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.470
He's being completely open about this...

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:42.110
Yes, this guy is just like Itsuki.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:43.050
Except...

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:47.580
In short, no matter what the reason
for your coming here, it's fruitless.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.080
Hold it!

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:53.330
It's true that, so long as I remain a witch,

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:55.590
nothing about me is pure.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.060
My body and soul are stained with magic.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.770
I neither resent nor bemoan that fact.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:04.070
However!

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:10.470
No, because of that,
my heart belongs purely to Itsuki.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.510
I won't surrender what's in my heart.

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:17.010
That is the one truth I have.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.650
My, you've really fallen hard for him,
haven't you?

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.780
What is it that so appealing about this boy?

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.560
I finally understand.

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:32.120
You don't have anyone that's
important to you, do you?

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:39.100
Where or what has nothing
to do with loving someone.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:42.080
And so, the moment you said those words,

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.840
you became absurd to me.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.740
You aren't like Itsuki at all.

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.250
I have no reason to speak with you any further.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:52.810
Just tell me where Honami is!

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:54.250
And if I say no?

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:57.050
Then I'll tear it out of you!

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:14.540
Trying to recover everyone, are you?

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.970
However, why don't I keep Itsuki here with me?

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:18.940
Hail!

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:23.910
Itsuki!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.290
Oh, a dragon?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:46.000
Magical things really do like you, don't they?

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.050
Big Sister Adelicia! Uncle Sekiren!

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.020
Are you okay?!

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:02.350
It's nothing serious.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.190
But really, "Uncle"?

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:07.890
Why did you have to interfere,
you miserly Onmyouji?!

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:11.100
I'd hoped to bring the president back with you.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:12.860
So, our adversary is...

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:16.000
Fin Cruda. A Changeling.

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:18.000
A changeling?

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:22.710
There are legends that fairies
steal newborn children away.

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:25.710
Like the Japanese legends of
being spirited away, right?

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:32.750
What the children see in the other world
leaves an effect on their minds and bodies.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:35.350
For example, Glam Sight.

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:37.090
But...

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:41.460
Yes. Fin Cruda possesses Glam Sight, like Itsuki.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:43.560
I see.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:49.490
But what is he trying to accomplish by
drawing out the dragon fragment?

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.540
A sacrifice.

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:59.740
That idiot Honami and Fin are going
to sacrifice it to cure Itsuki's eye.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.290
This has gotten very bad.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:22.540
We should have handed over the dragon
to The Association before it grew,

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:25.530
but instead Astral hid and sealed it.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:32.280
He and Honami are drawing the fragment
out again and trying to hatch it.

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.690
If The Association knew about this,

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:43.820
they'd destroy Astral, and Honami would
be punished for breaking a taboo.

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:46.730
Besides that, sacrificing a dragon!

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:51.520
That's dangerous magic, and could
cost Miss Honami her life.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:04.440
Scared?

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.450
I'm okay.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:09.150
I'm a mage, after all.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:09.770
Huh?

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:13.180
Besides, you're special, aren't you, Icchan?

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:16.260
Come on, let's go.

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:50.280
Icchan?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:55.020
Over here! Catch me if you can!

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:04.460
Don't... DON'T!!!

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:22.850
Who?

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.420
Who am I?

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:38.160
Who am I?

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.570
Who am I?

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.610
Are you... a dragon?

00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:52.110
Are you a dragon?

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:54.780
Who am I?

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.620
Icchan?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:15.840
Icchan?

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:20.510
Icchan!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:22.910
Icchan...

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.790
NO!!!

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:51.140
Icchan!

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.370
Icchan!

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:54.950
I'm okay.

00:20:57.280 --> 00:20:59.380
Really, I'm okay.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.350
I'm okay.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:07.760
So, please, Acchan...

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.030
Acchan...

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:22.770
Are you ready, Honami?

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:28.470
Hail!

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.480
Dragon of the slumbering earth!

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:34.020
By the sacrifice of the descendant
of the sacred tree, awaken!

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:53.270
Let us begin the sacrifice of the dragon.

00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:20.790
Over and over, holding my wounded hand...
Kizutsuku te wo nandomo tsunaide

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:29.200
...you walk this uncertain path with me...
fuan bakari no kono michi wo aruite

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:42.250
...amidst the days as they slowly drift by.
yukkuri nagareta hibi no naka de bokura ga

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:54.170
The things we obtain are so warm, so beloved.
Te ni shita mono wa konna ni atatakute itoshinda

00:22:54.170 --> 00:23:00.440
Please, as time goes by, let's keep right on...
Nee konomama toki no naka

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:04.940
...laughing and walking together.
waratte aruite yukou

00:23:05.810 --> 00:23:09.220
It's because you're with me...
Kimi ga iru kara

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:14.310
...that I can keep moving forward.
mae ni susumerunda

00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:26.190
Now our feelings are becoming one...
Ima bokura no omoi ga hitotsu ni natte

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:30.240
...and showing the path to us.
michi wo shimesunda

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:34.510
So please, keep on holding my hand...
Dakara kono te zutto

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:37.570
...and never let it go...
hanasanaide

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:39.850
CHANGELING [CHANGELING]

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:42.080
CHANGELING [CHANGELING]
This is a creature that
fairies replace a child with.

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:43.350
CHANGELING [CHANGELING]
What happens to the child it replaces?

00:23:43.550 --> 00:23:44.570
I don't know.

00:23:44.680 --> 00:23:46.750
If things go well, the child is returned, but...

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:47.990
I hope they bring it back.

00:23:47.990 --> 00:23:50.180
Naïve as always, Itsuki.

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:51.660
What do you think, Prof. Miwa?

